  - Navigation: ChatDetail route with impersonatedEntityId for roleplay support
  - QoL Features: Last message actions (delete/edit/regenerate), new messages tracking, mark-as-read, async transcription editing, reply mode toggle
- Phase 3: Audio Playback Bug Fix & Duration Enrichment
  - Root Cause Fixed: Removed `preloadAudio` useEffect from ChatBubble that caused a race condition where all audio bubbles simultaneously called `AudioPlayer.loadAudioForMessage()` on mount after reconnect, corrupting the singleton TrackPlayer queue.
  - AudioPlayer: Added static `getDurationFromBase64(base64Audio, mimeType)` using `music-metadata` v11 (replaced deprecated `music-metadata-browser`); parses audio duration from buffer without any TrackPlayer interaction.
  - EntitySessionService: After saving an incoming TTS audio message with no duration, immediately parses and persists `audio_duration` to DB via `updateConversationMessage`.
  - ChatDetailScreen: On load, runs a best-effort `Promise.all` enrichment loop for any historical messages that have `audio_data` but no `audio_duration`; persists to DB so subsequent loads are instant.
  - ChatBubble: No DB writes at all; duration displayed from `message.audio_duration` prop (from DB) on initial render, then updated to live TrackPlayer value once playback starts.
- Phase 2: Dual Entity Chat Session Reconnection Hardening
  - EntitySessionService: Added disconnected:entity listener → session status updated immediately on entity WS drop; no more phantom "Connected" state after Harmony Link restart.
  - EntitySessionService.startDualSession: Detects stale (disconnected) sessions in the sessions map and fully cleans them up before creating fresh connections instead of silently returning the dead session.
  - EntitySessionService: Extracted cleanupTranscriptionsForPartner() helper, reused across stopSession() and handleEntityDisconnected().
  - SyncConnectionContext: Replaced reconnectTimeoutId React state with useRef; added isPairedRef/isConnectingRef/isReconnectingRef/isConnectedRef mirroring their state counterparts; all event handlers read from refs so closures are never stale. Single useEffect with empty deps [].
  - EntitySessionContext: Removed activeSessions.size from sync-drop effect deps; calls entitySessionService.closeAllSessions() directly (authoritative service map, not stale React state).
  - ChatDetailScreen: Split single "init + cleanup" useEffect into two effects: (1) unmount-only lifecycle effect (stops session on screen navigation); (2) isConnected-reactive init effect (restarts session on reconnect, no stopDualSession in cleanup). Eliminates double-stop race condition.
- Safe Area Bottom Insets: Android system navigation bar safe area padding applied to all scrollable screens and ChatInput.
- Session Resume: Sessions auto-resume on disconnect; dangling events reconciled with clients on reconnect.
- Instant vs. Realistic Reply Times: Per-chat-partner reply mode toggle persisted via AsyncStorage; defaults to "realistic".
- Emoji Features: Full emoji picker (native/Twemoji/Noto sets), EmojiAction system with Ekman8 emotion effects, entity-level action customization, DB migrations 22-23, emoji_actions repository, EmojiContext provider, emoji autocomplete in ChatInput, emoji-rich text rendering.
- Interactions Data Layer: Interaction model (mirrors Go struct), interactions.repository (full CRUD, JOIN queries, participant key derivation), migrations 24-28 (interactions table, drop session_id, interaction summary, memory lifecycle fields, presence_type).
- Session Refactor to InteractionSession: DualEntitySession replaced by InteractionSession; events keyed by interactionId (not partnerEntityId); supports N participants per session.
- UI Adaptation: ChatListScreen and ChatDetailScreen adapted to InteractionSession model; JOIN-based queries for chat list previews.
- Force Full DB Sync: Option in SyncSettingsScreen to trigger full re-synchronization.
- Cleanup: Deprecated methods removed, review fixes applied, codebase map updated.
- Provider Expansion + Model Unification (Complete): Full xAI/Google/Anthropic provider support, model field consolidation, dead code cleanup across app.
- Dynamic Atmospheric Background (Complete): Aurora/Nebula animated background with 5 gradient blobs + 40 stardust particles. Uses theme accent colors (Neon Magenta/Indigo). Prime-number cycle durations prevent visible loops. Persistent layer behind entire navigation stack. Navigation contentStyle set to transparent for glassmorphism effect. Components: DynamicAtmosphericBackground.tsx, StardustParticles.tsx in src/components/background/.
  - Migration 000030: DB migration adds Google/xAI/Anthropic config tables; unifies model columns (`embedding_model`/`image_model`/`imagination_model` → `model`).
  - providers.ts: 21 provider CRUD functions (15 providers). Restored + fixed after garbled state. Fixed `module_` prefixed table bug for 8 providers. Added xAI/Google/Anthropic CRUD functions.
  - providerFieldSchemas.ts: 15 provider schemas. Module-specific fields merged into main provider schemas with tooltips. Dead module-specific schema keys removed.
  - ModuleConfigEditScreen.tsx: PROVIDER_REPOSITORIES map + OPENAI_FAMILY array includes all 15 providers. Google/xAI/Anthropic import + config support.
  - moduleConfiguration.ts: Movement providerOptions includes Google/xAI/Anthropic.
  - moduleDefaults.ts: PROVIDER_DEFAULTS has all provider entries. Movement defaults for Google/xAI/Anthropic (maxtokens: 200).
  - Unified `isInUse` to shared `isProviderConfigInUse()` helper — single UNION ALL query.
- Soulbits API Client Adoption (Complete): `CloudSessionService` (session broker connect/disconnect + poll loop) refactored to use the first-party `@harmony-ai-solutions/soulbits-api-client` via new `src/services/cloud/soulbitsClient.ts` factory `buildSoulbitsClient({paseto})` — PASETO-only (no refreshToken) so 401 refresh stays in `AuthService` (one persisted credential for REST + WS). App keeps its own poll loop on the client's `session.connect()` primitive (not `connectPoll`) to preserve the state machine + UI + cancel contract; `session.disconnect(sid)` for grace-period RPC. Public API of CloudSessionService unchanged → no consumer edits. `config/cloud.ts`: added `CLOUD_HOSTS.session`, removed dead `AUTH_ENDPOINTS.sessionConnect/sessionDisconnect`; `authFetch.ts` now orphaned (left in place). 14/14 unit tests pass.
- Soulbits API Client — dependency source fixed: migrated from a local `file:../soulbits-api-client-js` link (plus an untracked `.npmrc` with `install-links=true` that copied the local folder into node_modules, never touching GitHub) to a proper GitHub git dependency pinned to client commit `518c9e8`. Client repo gained a `prepare` script (`npm run build` → tsup) so npm builds the gitignored `dist/` on git-install. `package-lock.json` now resolves the git URL + commit + integrity hash; `.npmrc` deleted. To bump the client: commit+push it, then re-pin the app commit SHA and run `npm install` (no npm publish).
